course: dictionary
lesson: 1021
title: One small word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word boo can do different jobs. It can be a shout, an action word, or a sound you hear. The words around it tell you which job it is doing. «Boo!» shouted from behind a door is a shout to give someone a fright.
explain: As a verb, boo is an action: «The crowd began to boo the referee.» The clue is the crowd. Booed means they shouted boo to show they did not like him. As a noun, a boo is the sound itself: «The match ended with a loud boo from the stands.»
explain: Context also shows how the word feels. In the sentence about matches, booing is not fair, and booing your own players knocks their confidence. So here boo is not a joke. It is unkind. Ask yourself: is this a fright, a sign of dislike, or a kind pet name? Then check that your meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Boo is a word you shout to make someone jump or get a fright.
fact: To boo someone means to shout «boo» to show you do not like a performer, player or speaker.
fact: A boo is a sound of dislike from a crowd.
fact: Boo can also be a pet name for someone you love, used informally.
fact: The phrase «wouldn't say boo to a goose» means someone is very shy.
exercise: «Boo!» jumped out from behind the door, and Sam screamed. What is boo doing here? | * A shout to give someone a fright | A sound of dislike from a crowd | A cheer for the winning team | A pet name for a friend
exercise: «The crowd began to boo the referee after the disputed goal.» What does boo mean here? | To tell him a joke | * To shout boo to show dislike | To give him a hug | To cheer loudly for him
exercise: In «Ben heard a loud boo from the stands», what kind of word is boo? | A verb, an action word | A question word | A place name | * A noun, the sound of dislike from the crowd
test: Mum calls her little boy «my boo» in a kind way. What does boo mean here? | A sound of anger from a crowd | * A pet name for someone you love | A shout to frighten | A ghost
test: The sentence says booing your own players is unkind. Why? | It helps them run faster | * It knocks their confidence | It makes the referee happy | It makes the game shorter
exam: What does the phrase «wouldn't say boo to a goose» mean? | Very hungry | Very loud | Very angry | * Very shy
